commit 3c1814f2ee26fc99cb92b0d5ea5f5d5b98be370d
Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Wed Jun 4 18:26:55 2025 +0200
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Wed Jun 4 18:26:55 2025 +0200

    Bug 1970044 - Move schema annotations into the tree. r=freaktechnik




    The main goal of this effort is to make the tree the only source of
    information for our WebExtension APIs. Our documentation is
    mostly generated from the schema files, but we are still not able
    to auto-generate it. Information has to be updated in different places,
    none of which is documented.

    This patch moves most of the information stored in "overlay" files in
    the `webext-docs` repository [1] into annotation files. The concept
    itself is also changed: The overlay files could replace descriptions and
    other properties, which could hide updated information in the schema
    files. The new concept it to extend the schema with additional
    information.

    In the past we tried to minimize the usage of overlay files and stuffed
    as much as we can into the schema description. This led to
    usage of undocumented tags in the descriptions, like <lituralinclude>,
    <codeblock> and others. We also ended up with line breaks (\n) in the
    schema description in order to format the generated documentation. The
    annotation concept uses an array of well defined annotation objects, and
    this patch moves all these "quirks" out of the schema descriptions into
    annotation objects. Consumers can now decide, if they want to use just
    the main description, or any of the additional information available
    through annotation objects.

    We also no longer have to dublicate an entire API definition for
    Manifest V2 and Manifest V3 *just* to be able to provide different
    descriptions (see the commands API).

    This patch also introduces the `url-placeholder.json` file, which holds
    the information currently hardcoded in the `webext-schemas-generator`
    repository [2]. We also introduce a well documented macro to use these
    placeholders: `$(url:<name>)`. This is in line with the already
    used macros `$(ref:<name>)`, `$(doc:<name>)` and `$(topic:<name>)`
    introduced by mozilla-central. We decided to follow mozilla-central and
    no longer use `<a>` tags in the schemas, but the shorthand notation
    `$(url:<name>)[Title]`.

    We still use tags like `<code>`, `<var>` and `<em>`. This will be
    revisetted later.

    The path forward is to update the `webext-schemas-generator` to include
    the additional information in our post-processed schema files, and then
    introduce a `webext-docs-generator` which will use that data to
    auto-generate the docs, without any further manual interaction.

    [1]:https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-docs/tree/56f005c0eb1c7433b50efe730a6c441882213cdc/overlay
    [2]:https://github.com/thunderbird/webext-schemas-generator/blob/3f1a8438dfc23a83376394502b07aa667bbc2822/get_thunderbird_schema_files.js#L78-L137

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D252284

